# s3-06 (+ g25-fu-cu-a): fill_saved_login served by the core (SavedLoginComputerBackend)

The re-exports in mixdog-core-session secret_input.rs (SavedLoginComputerBackend, SavedLoginTurnClock, SavedLoginTurns,
SettlingSavedLogins) are in the tree. What is left is the daemon composition, all in
[mixdog-app-server-daemon/src/compose_flip.rs]. Every name below is real; nothing is a placeholder.

1. Before `let fill = ...SecretFill::new(` (the "ONE secret fill" block) nothing is needed. Right AFTER `let fill = Arc::new(match &browser_timing { ... });`
   add the one registry, the redactor over it and the turn clock:

    let saved_logins = mixdog_core_session::session::secret_input::SavedLoginRegistry::new();
    let saved_login_turns = mixdog_core_session::session::secret_input::SavedLoginTurnClock::new(saved_logins.clone());
    let redactor: Arc<dyn mixdog_core_session::session::secret_input::Redact> = Arc::new(mixdog_core_session::session::secret_input::FullRedactor { saved: saved_logins.clone(), sessions: fill.clone() });

2. In the `computer_pool` session closure (the one that builds RedactingComputerBackend then GatedComputerBackend): capture
   `(fill, human_only, redactor, saved_logins, saved_login_turns, late_computer_hosts, host)` where `host = b.host.clone()`, build the
   redacting backend with `redactor.clone()` in place of `fill.clone()` (so saved-login passwords are hidden from every computer reply),
   and wrap the gated backend:

    let gated = Arc::new(mixdog_core_session::session::secret_input::GatedComputerBackend::new(redacted, human_only.clone()));
    Arc::new(mixdog_core_session::session::secret_input::SavedLoginComputerBackend::new(
        gated,
        mixdog_core_api::ids::ThreadId::from(session),
        mixdog_tools::desktop::host::ChannelHostCommands::new(host.clone()),  // `new` returns Arc<Self> already
        Arc::new(mixdog_core_session::session::secret_input::HostComputerCommands::new(late_computer_hosts.clone(), human_only.clone())),
        saved_logins.clone(),
        redactor.clone(),
        saved_login_turns.clone(),
    )) as Arc<dyn mixdog_core_api::domain::computer::ComputerBackend>

   (The vault's answer is consumed by the fill and never reaches a model, so the desktop channel needs no redaction.)

3. In the `SessionDeps` literal, the `snapshots:` field (the `match &computer_pool { Some(pool) => Arc::new(SettlingSnapshots::new(..)), None => worktree_snapshots }` block):
   wrap the whole block's value, so a settled turn and a stopped runtime reach the registry:

    snapshots: Arc::new(mixdog_core_session::session::secret_input::SettlingSavedLogins::new({ <the existing block, unchanged> }, saved_login_turns.clone())),

   This is what lifts the pixel guard and the password redaction (`settle` on `turn_settled`, `forget` on `runtime_stopped`); without it
   the first password fill would hold captures back for the daemon's life.

[handoff env] where `fill.clone()` is passed as the redactor that hides tool replies of the handoff env, pass `redactor.clone()` instead.

[SERVICE_PENDING] nothing to remove: fill_saved_login is a computer action, not a protocol method; `host/browser/command` saved_login_* already exists.
